## Goals
- A runnable example for each feature area that has none: chart trendlines and error bars,
  chart 3D view and wall/floor formatting, master→layout→slide placeholder inheritance,
  and picture effects.
- Every new script re-opens the `.pptx` it wrote and asserts the round-tripped values match
  what was written — a script that only saves proves nothing.
- Round-trip asserts added to `examples/add_chart_secondary_axis.py`, which already exists.
- README "Examples" table lists every script; each new script's module docstring points back
  to the `.claude/context/feature-manifest.md` section it demonstrates.

## Objectives / acceptance
- `python examples/<name>.py` exits 0 for every script, from a clean working directory.
- Each new script's assertions are bare `assert`s against values read back from the reopened
  file, and each has been seen to fail (checked by perturbing an expected value once).
- `pytest -q` stays at 3657 passed; CI green on all 7 cells.
- `ls examples/` and the README "Examples" table list the same files.
- No new public API on this branch. Gaps found are filed for v0.4.0, not patched here.
